# JPM In-Store (semi-integrated) configuration — Android / Gradle
#
# Android projects do NOT use .env files. Store these values in the project's
# `local.properties` (already gitignored by default in a standard Android
# project) and surface them to app code as BuildConfig fields.
#
# Add the `jpm.*` keys below to your existing `local.properties`, fill in the
# values from your onboarding artifacts, and do NOT commit real values.

# --- Terminal connection ---------------------------------------------------
# The terminal exposes a TLS WebSocket the POS connects to.
# Real terminal listening port is 8442. Use the terminal's LAN IP.
#   wss://<terminal-ip>:8442
jpm.terminal.host=
jpm.terminal.port=8442

# --- Mandatory terminal identifier -----------------------------------------
# HWVENDORID is assigned by J.P. Morgan and MUST be set at startup via the
# SetParameter operation BEFORE any transaction. Placeholder only — fill from
# your onboarding artifacts. Do not commit the real value.
jpm.hwvendorid=

# --- Environment -----------------------------------------------------------
# CAT = Customer Acceptance Testing (JPM test environment). PROD = production.
# Go-live to PROD is gated by JPM validation.
jpm.env=CAT

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Wiring into BuildConfig (build.gradle.kts) — read the keys at build time and
# expose them so no host/identifier is hardcoded in source:
#
#   import java.util.Properties
#
#   val localProps = Properties().apply {
#       val f = rootProject.file("local.properties")
#       if (f.exists()) f.inputStream().use { load(it) }
#   }
#
#   android {
#       buildFeatures { buildConfig = true }
#       defaultConfig {
#           buildConfigField("String", "JPM_TERMINAL_HOST",
#               "\"${localProps.getProperty("jpm.terminal.host", "")}\"")
#           buildConfigField("String", "JPM_TERMINAL_PORT",
#               "\"${localProps.getProperty("jpm.terminal.port", "8442")}\"")
#           buildConfigField("String", "JPM_HWVENDORID",
#               "\"${localProps.getProperty("jpm.hwvendorid", "")}\"")
#           buildConfigField("String", "JPM_ENV",
#               "\"${localProps.getProperty("jpm.env", "CAT")}\"")
#       }
#   }
#
# Then read them in app code via BuildConfig.JPM_TERMINAL_HOST, etc.
